    "notes": "1. When was the SAT first administered to high-school students? A  1887 B  1901 C  1914 D  1926 E  1943  2. What was the first university to require its applicants to take the SAT? A  Dartmouth B  George Washington C  Harvard D  Princeton E  UC Berkeley  3. Which test was not created by the Educational Testing Service (ETS)? A  ACT B  GRE C  MAPP D  SAT E  TOEFL  4. The maximum score on an LSAT is 180. What's the minimum score? A  0 B  40 C  90 D  100 E  120  5. Which GRE subject test was phased out in 2000 due to declining numbers of testees? A  Computer Science B  History C  Literature in English D  Mathematics E  Psychology  BONUS QUESTION: What group has benefited most from standardized testing? (To find the answer, read the Down entries that intersect the correct answers to the five questions above.)"
